  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "What is the value of the following expression?\n\n\\[(2^0-1+5^2+0)^{-1} \\times 5\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-125\\)",
    "B": "\\(-120\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\)",
    "E": "\\(25\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "A nonzero number raised to the zeroth power equals \\(1\\), so \\(2^0=1\\). Evaluating the powers inside the parentheses gives\n\\[\n2^0-1+5^2+0=1-1+25+0=25.\n\\]\nBecause \\(25\\neq0\\), its power \\(-1\\) is its reciprocal. Thus the expression equals\n\\[\n25^{-1}\\cdot5=\\frac{1}{25}\\cdot5=\\boxed{\\frac15},\n\\]\nchoice C.",
